      "source": "hackerearth",
      "standard_solution_code": "def is_enlightenment_possible(ar, n, k, dist):\n\t#Checks if all n temples in list ar is possible to be enlightened by k monks with range dist\n\tpos = ar[0] + dist\n\tfor i in ar:\n\t\tif abs(pos - i) > dist:\n\t\t\tk = k - 1\n\t\t\tpos = i + dist\n\tk = k - 1\n\tif k >= 0:\treturn True\n\treturn False\n\n\nN, K = list(map(int, input().split()))\nar = list(map(int, input().split()))\nar.sort()\nlo, hi = 1, 10000000\nans = 0\nwhile lo<=hi:\n\tmid = (lo + hi) >> 1\n\t#print '%d .. %d .. %d' %(lo, mid, hi)\n\tif is_enlightenment_possible(ar, N, K, mid):\n\t\tans = mid\n\t\thi = mid - 1\n\telse:\n\t\tlo = mid + 1\nprint(ans)"
    }
